If the issue is colons in names, rsync treats colons specially only in the first path component. For relative paths, prepend `./` so rsync won’t interpret the colon as a host separator.

Example:
`rsync -av ./sou:rce/ ./de:st/`

In a script, you can do:
```sh
case $source in
  /*) :;;
  *) source=./$source;;
esac
case $dest in
  /*) :;;
  *) dest=./$dest;;
esac
rsync "$source" "$dest"
```

If you meant a different kind of name/path change beyond colons, this only covers how to avoid rsync misreading colons as remote syntax.

