You can rename dynamically in Perl by reading each filename and applying a regex before calling `rename`:

```perl
#!/usr/bin/perl
opendir(DIR, ".") or die "$@:$!";
while ($in = readdir(DIR)) {
  next unless -f $in;
  ($out = $in) =~ s/[^a-zA-Z0-9._-]//g;
  warn "$@:$!" unless rename $in, $out;
}
closedir(DIR);
```

This removes characters outside `a-zA-Z0-9._-`. It does not preserve spaces or umlauts, so if you want to keep regular UTF-8 characters or spaces, the regex would need to be adjusted.

